@title Status chip: the heat run is in sight in 3D and the Cabinet, with every panel closed
@area 3D
@sizes 1366x768 1920x1080
# The chip (now a status bar slot, #1811) of the 3D view and the Cabinet reads the one heat status: not run, running with Cancel, done. It is there with the Heat panel closed, and the Cabinet shows the same words (docs/design/visual-redesign-3d.md section 4).
open qa/fixtures/cabinet-cooling-advice.novo
wait 20
click_text 3D #1
wait 30
expect "Heat not run"
shot 3d-not-run
check_layout
click_text Heat #1
wait 20
# Opening Heat on a small cabinet starts an automatic run, which greys out the Quality row: stop it first.
click_text Cancel
wait 10
# With Auto on a stopped run starts again at once and greys out the Quality row: switch Auto off.
click_text Auto #1
wait 10
# The run that Auto had started again is still going: stop it too.
try click_text Cancel
wait 10
click_text "Settings for the next run"
wait 10
click_text Quick
wait 10
shot 3d-heat-panel-open
check_layout
click_text "Heat not run"
wait 40
expect_not "Heat not run"
shot 3d-running
check_layout
wait_s 100
wait 60
wait_s 100
wait 60
expect "Heat done"
shot 3d-done
check_layout
click_text Cabinet #1
wait 30
expect "Heat done"
shot cabinet-done
check_layout
